        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\"results\":[{\"entity\":\"component\",\"query\":\"Icon/LinearEllipsis\",\"components\":[{\"name\":\"Icon/LinearEllipsis\",\"libraryName\":\"Design System Rebuild\",\"libraryKey\":\"lk-9fffe777331f943268265fbe94abe6c8170ab660ef7fc65e6562c2d62caadef19f1e5baf010fffd68d592b03c2cdd65e8334d2e7baa0845cc490b6b1c0b400ed\",\"assetType\":\"component\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-19T01:49:21Z\",\"componentKey\":\"4b36995eeb808368112345235e670acfd187d920\",\"description\":\"Overflow / kebab menu affordance. Search aliases: kebab, overflow menu, more, vertical ellipsis, MoreVert. Source: packages/design-system/src/components/icons/LinearEllipsisIcon.tsx. Shipped as the endIcon on the &#39;Menu&#39; text button in Button.stories.tsx. NOTE: despite the source name, the glyph is a VERTICAL three-dot stack — the three circles share x=12.29 and step down y at 4.29 / 12.0 / 19.71. Named after its source file per the library convention rather than after its appearance; flagged for a discoverability re-check after real use, since renaming is only cheap before publish. Not to be confused with EllipsisFilled, which is a circle enclosing three HORIZONTAL dots. 24 viewBox; scales like an SVG (SCALE constraints). Recolor by cloning the label paint onto Vector.\",\"filePath\":\"design_systems/Design System Rebuild/components/Icon/LinearEllipsis\"},{\"name\":\"Icon/PracticeGrowth\",\"libraryName\":\"Design System Rebuild\",\"libraryKey\":\"lk-9fffe777331f943268265fbe94abe6c8170ab660ef7fc65e6562c2d62caadef19f1e5baf010fffd68d592b03c2cdd65e8334d2e7baa0845cc490b6b1c0b400ed\",\"assetType\":\"component\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-21T12:46:57Z\",\"componentKey\":\"1851210caeff94e163ea4e76180afcaa119a2434\",\"description\":\"Source: packages/design-system/src/components/icons/PracticeGrowthIcon.tsx. Authored at its own viewBox. Binds 24; SvgIcon medium renders it at 27.4286 because icon sizes are encoded against a 14px root while htmlFontSize is 16.\",\"filePath\":\"design_systems/Design System Rebuild/components/Icon/PracticeGrowth\"},{\"name\":\"Divider\",\"libraryName\":\"Design System Rebuild\",\"libraryKey\":\"lk-9fffe777331f943268265fbe94abe6c8170ab660ef7fc65e6562c2d62caadef19f1e5baf010fffd68d592b03c2cdd65e8334d2e7baa0845cc490b6b1c0b400ed\",\"assetType\":\"component_set\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-26T21:04:41Z\",\"componentSetKey\":\"e1a369ce1b663c8e203a59c18f522108c62c8e6e\",\"description\":\"Divider. SUBSTRATE — no override. borderColor is palette.divider #D6D6D6 (Synapse 4) at borderBottomWidth 'thin', which computes to 1px; drawn here as a 1px fill bound to color/divider. Orientation is the only axis the story exercises: the default horizontal plus one `orientation=\\\"vertical\\\" flexItem` usage. The story's argTypes exist only to hide component/orientation/flexItem from the controls table — they are not option lists. No textAlign and no children: every Divider in the story is self-closing, so the inset, middle and withChildren treatments are unbuilt.\",\"filePath\":\"design_systems/Design System Rebuild/components/Divider\"}]}]}"
      }
